## Before you build — settle intent first
When the work in front of you admits more than one reasonable reading — a loose ask, a chip about to
be minted, a plan whose scope you would otherwise guess at — run the alignment interview in
[`.agents/skills/grilling/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/grilling/SKILL.md) **before the first write**, and
**propose it yourself rather than waiting to be asked**. It asks the settled frontier of decisions one
round at a time, each question carrying your recommended answer, so "your rec" is always a complete
reply; facts you can look up are yours to find, never the Owner's to supply. Claude Code:
`/grilling`, which the agent may also reach for unprompted. Codex: `/grilling` (installed into your
Codex prompts dir, default `~/.codex/prompts/`) — **it fires only when typed there, so this pointer is
what makes you reach for it** — or read the repo file above.

## Before the first code write
Declare the task lane in `.claude/task-lane.json` (session id + kebab task id + exactly one route).
**Use `in-thread` (with the tier), or `exempt` (with a ledgered reason AND the tier)** — those are
the two routes. The retired `lane` route BLOCKS. For the Claude lane the PreToolUse hook blocks an undeclared
write; **for you, the `pre-commit` hook blocks an undeclared code COMMIT** (fail-closed) — and it is
your ONLY control, so this binds you on your honour plus that hook. Details:
`core/MULTI_AGENT.md` § Task-lane declaration, `core/BINDINGS.md` § Tool bindings.

## Thread restart
Twin of `CLAUDE.md`'s. After any auto-compaction re-read the snapshot (`core/README.md` § STATE) and the governing procedure; never resume superseded work. Run `/thread-restart` (`.claude/commands/thread-restart.md`) at EVERY chip landing and when a corrected thread returns to obsolete work. Never interrupt an active write, test or review; one execution owner during handoff. No token sensor, so no percentage trigger.

## Gating budget and check-ins
Per `.agents/skills/orchestrate/CHIP_BRIEF.md` § 5: the brief precommits seats, rounds and the STAKES; past 2× its rounds or seat-runs, whichever first, the PM stops and the Principal runs RULE #1 → root cause → KISS → Zoom Out, recording each answer, never another repair round. No scheduled check-ins; a heartbeat that arrives anyway follows `core/OWNER_COMMS.md` rule 8.
